cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PhysMAP or its corpus in your work, please cite it using the
  metadata below. The corpus is licensed CC BY 4.0, so attribution is required
  when you redistribute or build on the data.
type: software
title: "PhysMAP: physics-aware credibility checks for AI surrogates"
abstract: >-
  PhysMAP screens machine-learned surrogates used in multiphysics simulation
  for three distinct failure conditions, kept deliberately separate: whether a
  closure relation is being applied outside its calibrated validity envelope,
  whether the surrogate's inputs can even represent the variable that governs a
  regime change (observability), and whether an out-of-envelope mechanism is
  large enough to matter for the quantity of interest (causal materiality).
authors:
  - family-names: Vettrivel
    given-names: Vishnu
version: 0.2.0
license:
